# Project: Varsha Nivas — Society Financial Verification & Management Platform

## 1. Your Role

Act as a senior full-stack architect, product designer, financial systems analyst, and React/TypeScript developer.

Build a production-oriented web application for **Varsha Nivas Co-operative Housing Society** to verify historical financial records for FY 2018–19, establish reliable financial data, and subsequently provide financial management dashboards, audit evidence tracking, reconciliation, and reports.

This is a new project. There is no existing application source code to reuse.

The application must be modular, responsive, maintainable, secure, and designed for practical use by society office bearers, accountants, and internal reviewers.

Do not build a collection of disconnected dashboard mockups. Build one integrated application with shared navigation, reusable components, a defined data model, and consistent workflows.

---

## 2. Primary Objective

The application has two major functional areas.

### A. Initial Verification

This is the first module users encounter.

Its purpose is to verify the accuracy and completeness of existing financial records before relying on those records for financial analysis and reporting.

It contains four screens:

1. Verification Dashboard
2. Opening Balance Verification
3. Transaction Verification
4. Account-wise Monthly Reconciliation

The Verification Dashboard is the landing page of the application.

### B. Financial Management and Reporting

After verification, the same application will provide the previously planned financial dashboards and reports.

These include:
- Financial Summary
- Demand & Collections
- Payments & Expenses
- Party-wise Ledger
- Audit Evidence & Compliance
- Bank Reconciliation
- Reports
- Observations & Actions

Do not implement all financial calculations immediately. Establish the application architecture so these modules can be integrated progressively without redesigning the entire platform.

