# 8. SCREEN 3 — TRANSACTION VERIFICATION

Purpose: verify existing transaction records against physical vouchers, receipts, and bills.

The original transaction register already contains voucher and receipt numbers.

All bills, vouchers, and receipts are currently maintained in physical format.

**Do not build document uploads or a digital document repository in the initial version.**

### Filters

Provide:
- Financial Year
- Month
- Date range
- Account: All / Cash / TDCC / BOM
- Transaction Type: All / Receipt / Payment
- Evidence Status
- Internal Audit Status
- Search by date, party, description, voucher number, or receipt number

### Summary Cards

Display:
- Total Transactions
- Pending Verification
- Evidence Complete
- Evidence Discrepancies
- Missing Documents
- Internal Audit Failed

### Transaction Register

Display existing financial fields as read-only.

Columns:
- Transaction ID
- Date
- Account
- Transaction Type
- Party
- Description / Particulars
- Amount
- Voucher Number
- Receipt Number
- Bill Status
- Voucher / Receipt Status
- Evidence Status
- Internal Audit Status
- Remarks
- Action

Use the existing transaction reference fields. Do not generate duplicate voucher or receipt numbers.

### Bill Status

Allowed values:
- Available
- Discrepancy
- Missing
- N/A

### Voucher / Receipt Status

Allowed values:
- Available
- Discrepancy
- Missing

### Evidence Status

Calculate automatically.

Rules:
- Complete: all applicable documents are available.
- Missing: at least one applicable document is missing.
- Discrepancy: at least one applicable document has a discrepancy.
- Pending: required inspection fields have not been completed.
- N/A should apply only to document types that are genuinely not required for the transaction.

Define precedence consistently when multiple conditions occur.

For receipts, a purchase bill will normally be N/A. Do not flag a member receipt as missing an expense bill.

### Internal Audit Status

Allowed values:
- Pending
- Verified
- Failed

This is independent of Evidence Status.

A document can be physically available but contain an incorrect amount, date, party name, or purpose.

Such a transaction must be eligible for an Internal Audit result of Failed.

### Transaction Detail Panel

When a reviewer selects a transaction, display:
- All source transaction details
- Existing voucher and receipt references
- Applicable document inspection fields
- Internal audit result
- Remarks
- Reviewer identity
- Last updated timestamp

The reviewer physically locates the document, checks it against the transaction, and records the result.

### Save Rules

- Never alter the original financial amount through the inspection interface.
- Never silently modify the original transaction description, date, account, or voucher number.
- Save inspection fields separately.
- Require remarks for discrepancies and failures.
- Record changes in a change log.
- Prevent unauthorised users from modifying saved inspection results.

