# 11. Data Integrity and Verification Rules

The application must follow these principles.

1. Original financial records must be preserved.
2. Inspection results must be stored separately from financial source values.
3. Calculations must be formula-driven or calculated deterministically by the backend.
4. Source values and calculated values must never be silently overwritten.
5. Discrepancies must be visible and traceable.
6. Verification completion must not be inferred from arithmetic alone.
7. Missing documents and failed internal audits must remain separate statuses.
8. All significant changes must be attributable to a reviewer.
9. Avoid duplicate inspection records for the same transaction.
10. Use stable IDs and validate every backend update.
11. Prevent accidental concurrent overwrites where practical.
12. Clearly distinguish imported data from verified data.
13. Do not invent transaction records, account balances, audit results, or supporting documents.
14. Use an explicit reconciliation tolerance policy. Do not silently round away discrepancies.
15. Maintain an auditable correction process for any authorised changes to source data.

