# 12. Authentication and Security

This is an internal financial application.

Implement a defensible access model.

At minimum:
- Require authentication for application data access.
- Validate identity and permissions on the backend.
- Do not rely on hiding frontend buttons as an access-control mechanism.
- Do not expose unrestricted spreadsheet access to anonymous users.
- Keep credentials and sensitive configuration out of source code.
- Do not commit OAuth secrets, access tokens, or service credentials to GitHub.
- Validate input types and permitted field values on every write.
- Log sensitive modifications.
- Restrict spreadsheet and Drive permissions to authorised accounts.

Before production deployment, document the chosen authentication flow and how it is enforced by the backend.

Do not claim security is complete merely because a Google login button has been added.

